ms and modern  applications  and it can build that bridge in a secure  reliable  and scalable way so let's talk about  apigee apigee is google cloud's  api management platform not just an api  gateway  and it gives you all the tools you need  for unlocking your data via  apis apigee enables digital business  acceleration  with a unified and complete platform  purpose built for the digital economy  apigee makes it easier to manage the  entire digital value chain  with api services developer services and  analytics services  let's start at the bottom with api  services  this is the api runtime and mediation  engine  api services lets you manage the  connection between the api consumers  and the back-end service you have  complete control  over the request and the response you  can add security  transform requests and responses  orchestrate  calls across multiple systems impose  rate limits and quotas  and prevent people from abusing your  services  api analytics helps you measure tune  and monitor your api program it enables  end-to-end visibility  across the digital value chain with  developer analytics  operational and business metrics reports  about app performance  and custom reports that you may need all  are necessary to monitor  measure and manage success of your api  program  developer services enable a great  developer and community experience  that accelerates api adoption simplifies  learning and increases the business  value of  apis it provides a developer portal for  your api consumers  along with features for packaging  monetizing your services  and data when you're sharing your data  you want to make sure you do this in a  secure way  when we talk about security there are  many different aspects  for instance data should only reach the  right audience  this is where authentication and  authorization  come in in that respect apigee supports  widely used standards such as oauth and  openid connect  you also don't want anyone snooping  around when the data is in transit  this is where encryption plays a key  role  apigee supports tls mutual tls  and can support different configuration  of these protocols when communicating  with api clients and backend services  that hold the data  for example you may configure one-way  tls on the client  side but mutual tls for one of your  backends  and one way tls for another auditing is  also very important  you need to know who has accessed what  data who has made a change to the api  that exposes that data  apigee auditing and logging capabilities  have recovered  also is the sensitive data no problem  use an apigee extension  to quickly reduct data with gcp data  loss prevention services  you could potentially think of making  money out of your data as well  that is if you wish to of course not all  apis should necessarily be monetized  there are apis that build consumer  experience or drive  indirect value this should be free for  instance think about apis for ticket  booking  finding store locations product  availability etc  on the other hand if your apis help  developers  build apps that generate revenue you may  consider  charging for those apis for example  apis that provide weather data or  messaging services  apigee api monetization offers multiple  options to set up charge plans  you can configure fee based plans volume  based plans  you can set up revenue sharing with  developers freemium models  etc it also allows you to check  monetization plan limits during api  execution in short  whether you want to build new digital  experiences  create a partner ecosystem or apply  artificial intelligence or machine  learning to your data  unlocking your data is the key and apis  are the way to achieve this  we will now see how the australian  energy market operator  is unlocking its data and putting it to  effective work in an  ecosystem i'll now hand over to warren  thank you deb hello my name is warren  vala  and i am the enterprise integration  architect at the australian energy  market operator  today i'd like to talk through how aimo  has partnered with google  and the apogee platform to unlock the  power of our existing data  through apis we'll take a look at who  emo is  some of the unique challenges the energy  industry is facing  and how apis have been instrumental in  our digital transformation  so where does animo sit within the  australian energy market  aimo is responsible for the day-to-day  operations of the australian energy  market which is made up of multiple  markets covering both gas  and electricity on one side aimer  manages the physical nem grid  the transmission network the large  electricity towers that you may have  seen around the country  on the other side aimo operates the  financial energy markets to enable  energy flow  all the way from generation to the  customer households via retailers  as you can see some of the actors in the  energy markets are typical  large-scale generators such as coal  power plants and wind farms  all the way to meter data providers who  are responsible for sending the meter  data from households to aimo  sometimes this is automated via smart  meters and sometimes this is manually  read  one of the biggest shifts we are seeing  in the energy market is the active role  of the customer who is now  also playing a critical part of the grid  especially as power is starting to flow  two way  that's inter houses and now out of  houses  let's take a look at some of the  technology challenges that the energy  industry faces  if we look deeper into the national  electricity market which was built over  20 years ago  the systems are largely connected over  either scada operational systems over  private networks  or market data for example dispatch data  which is an instruction  sent to a generator every five minutes  all bids and offers into the market  which is received from generators and  retailers  is still sent over to aemo via batch  based systems over private networks  with the increase of dr penetration  across australia which is leading the  world  we have a unique opportunity to unlock  the value in our data  over modern protocols  and so what can animo do about this we  have a unique opportunity where we are  seeing an intersection  between the energy industry  transformation and our digital  transformation  and as part of our digital  transformation we are tapping into these  opportunities to enable new channels to  really lower the barrier entry  promoting further competition in the  market and as we digitize our systems  we are looking to foster innovation  within the energy market  especially in the space of distributed  energy more importantly we are seeing  the rise of prosumers who are looking to  take control of their energy profile  and play an active part in this energy  transformation  and so working with apogee has enabled  us to start this journey  as we look to reach a wider audience  our new apogee developer portal arms us  with the tools to create  a world-class developer experience  accelerate  api adoption simplify learning and  increase the business value of our apis  developers are the key consumers of our  apis and we want to provide them with a  great experience  and make it really easy for them to  discover understand  test and get going with our apis from  having an interactive sandbox to test  our apis  to letting developers manage their own  keys and access to the apis  and not necessarily in an open for all  approach but with the right guard rails  that apigee offers  our aperture developer portal has all  the tools the developer needs  to integrate with us let's take a look  at some of our large-scale programs with  opportunities to unlock the value  of our data the energy industry is  moving along with many programs centered  around a common theme in distributed  energy resources  starting with the distributed energy  resource register the dei register  allows registration of ddr assets  sitting behind the meter  for example rooftop solar panels and  household batteries  apis have enabled for this data to be  registered via the existing tools  and mobile applications that  electricians and installers are already  used to  the virtual power plant trial has  started to advance the integration of dr  into the national literacy market  allowing consumers to group together to  become a virtual power plant  apis have enabled for the management of  these vpps especially in the transfer of  telemetry data  and in the space of five minute  settlements the market is moving to more  granular data  and settlement down to five minutes apis  have enabled for a meter data  at five minute resolution to be sent  across the country  to ama's metadata management database  next we'll take a look at the cdr the  cdr is a national legislative program  which is running across multiple  industries  with the energy industry next in line  the cdr aims to give consumers better  access to their own data  and also allows competition by using a  data driven  innovation approach so let's take a look  at how we are using the apigee platform  to support the cdr  as a use case some of the key areas of  why apogee has been selected  was the choice of implementation options  especially with the hybrid option  giving us even more flexibility on where  to host our apis  whether that is in the google cloud  platform or in our private cloud  data sovereignty is especially important  as we operate national critical  infrastructure  and the flexibility of the platform  allows us to host the platform to make  our strict  obligations for the protection of our  data  and so the main focus of the apogee  platform is to manage our externally  facing apis  in the case of the cdp this allows us to  expose data from our metadata management  systems  and like most organizations we have data  spread over multiple cloud platforms  and on-prem systems and apogee allows us  to unify the experience when integrating  with our apis  apigee is truly enabling our digital  transformation  as we renovate our internal systems from  legacy integration protocols  to modern api ecosystems  now we'll take a look at a live demo and  explore how the victorian government  is using our apis to provide a  comparison service for australian  consumers  here we have an example of an external  consumer  the victorian government energy  comparison website who is consuming the  aimo cdp apis  to provide real-time meter data  retrieval from amaze metadata management  systems  and before the cdp apis were available  the end user needed to complete over 10  questions and in some cases a pdf bill  had to be uploaded  now that the api is available the user  only needs to know their national  metering identifier or their nimi and  the data is retrieved live from our api  i'll now hand it over to deb to walk us  through a live demo  the demo we're about to see is from the  point of view of a consumer wanting to  understand  which energy retailer offers the best  rates for the particular  electricity consumption patterns  i start looking around and i find a  public website that has been set up by  the government of victoria australia  when this website was first launched the  website would estimate the energy  consumption pattern  based on a series of answers provided by  the consumer  this was the simplest option but still  required  a lot of information to be provided the  other option was for the consumer to  upload  a pdf copy of the bill  i will now start answering all the  questions i am being asked  after providing this information i also  need to provide  details of my last electricity bill  at this point i can finally see which  rates are the most convenient to my  particular  situation but i had to answer more than  10  questions to get here and still it is  just an estimate  let us now see how apis that expose data  can improve my user experience  as well as provide more accurate results  so let's start again  this time i will choose a different  method for building my energy profile  quick and accurate this looks promising  all i need to provide is anemi this is a  unique identifier for the smart meter  installed in my house i can find it  in my electricity bill this option  is now powered by imo what this  means is that when i click on get my  data this website uses an  ammo api to retrieve the actual energy  consumption for my house in last 12  months  this provides a very accurate picture on  how i consume  energy  voila i can now see the rate space  suited to my household  without having to go through a lengthy  questionnaire i as a consumer  didn't even need to see the raw data  coming back from the api this user  experience is facilitated by the apis  published by imo  looking at amos api portal a developer  can easily find the relevant apis  and understand how to use them  in this demo we can appreciate the  advantages of unlocking data  via apis this is a public government  website  that leverages information held by aimo  to provide a  much better user experience not only are  the suggestions more  accurate to the consumer but also the  consumer can see them  in a couple of clicks thank you for  watching it  so what's next for aemo and apigee  one of our main focus areas is to enable  dr resources to be integrated into the  grid  which will increase api calls to  millions per day  as we start to receive more and more  telemetry data  and for the cdp api we are looking to  expand this service and enable data  service holders  to also provide data via the cdr gateway  model  we are always looking to reduce our  participant onboarding time and pivoting  off our developer portal to provide the  right amount of information  and further reduce the time to first  hello world  and of course our api product portfolio  is expanding as we continue to transform  our systems  as apis become our primary form of  integration  for our critical market systems thank  you for 